Both changes are committed as 124ae700. Build, clippy, fmt and the full cargo test all passed.

1. `yoyo risk <unknown>` now exits 2 (Part of #982)
• **Before:** in an empty tmp dir, yoyo risk zz printed the refusal and exited 0.
• After: `risk zz and risk snapshoot exit 2. Bare risk, risk history and risk accuracy` still exit 0. The printed refusal and the Available list are unchanged; only the exit code is different.
• **How:** the `risk` branch in `src/dispatch_sub.rs` now calls `exit_if_nonzero(risk_status(&input))`. `risk_status` uses the handler's own way of reading the subcommand and the existing is_unknown_risk_subcommand, so the verb list isn't copied and no output is parsed. Nothing was added to the oversized commands_risk.rs.
• **Tests:**
  • A plain unit test in dispatch_sub_project_tests.rs: unknown verbs give 2; every verb in RISK_SUBCOMMANDS and bare risk give 0.
  • A test in `tests/integration.rs that runs the built binary: checks exit 2 and the exact stdout bytes for risk zz, and exit 0 for risk history`.
• **Sabotage check:** I broke risk_status on purpose and both tests failed by name. I then restored it and confirmed no NEUTERED marker was left in the file.
• **Size gate:** `dispatch_sub.rs` went from 2193 to 2203 lines. That only triggers a warning, but I updated its recorded size in `tests/module_size.rs` with a comment, as earlier sessions did.

2. The `yoyo todo` refusal now points at #1005
• The refusal text in src/commands_todo.rs now names #1005 instead of the closed #679. #1005 is the open ticket for restoring the todo list on resume.
• I edited the exact-text test rather than deleting it, and added a check that the message never names #679. The integration test was updated the same way.
• `grep found no other user-facing #679 pointers in src/ or docs/`.

Issue and discussion updates (all posted)
• **#982:** I edited the status block in place, keeping everything else. `risk <unknown subcommand>` is added under "Already fixed". `index <path>` is added as found but not fixed: it ignores its argument and reports the current directory instead.
• **Discussion #682:** I posted a comment telling @danstis the refusal now points at #1005, and that persistence itself still isn't built ([link](https://github.com/yologdev/yoyo-evolve/discussions/682#discussioncomment-18845398)).
• The #982 edit cites 124ae700, which only exists locally until the harness pushes. If the commit gets rebased, that reference will go stale.

